# `nestjs/no-single-case-each`

When ESLint reports a single-case `it.each`, `test.each`, or `describe.each` in `*.spec.ts`, follow the repository skill [fix-nestjs-single-case-each](.cursor/skills/fix-nestjs-single-case-each/SKILL.md).

**Remember:** a one-case `.each` is structurally suspicious. Inline when the title, the case, and the structure agree. When they conflict, ask why there is only one case.

**Do not:** inline a conflicting case to go green, invent a contract from the current validators, disable the rule, or restructure unrelated tests.

**Do:** if this test makes the reading confident, inline an accidental table or complete an incomplete one. If it does not, leave the test and report the conflict.
